{{!--
Team progress or retro report for one period (week, month, quarter); readers are developers, team lead and product owner.
Read references/progress-reports.md before filling. Does not use the assessment partials.
progress: object with standing, limits, visual, delivered, attention, retro, followUps, numbers, method.
progress.standing: two or three short prose paragraphs; pace against elapsed time, what drives the gap, what it means for the plan; no bullets.
progress.limits: optional one sentence naming the caveat that changes how to read the report; leave out when none.
progress.visual: one or two fenced Mermaid charts (pie, xychart-beta) from supplied numbers, each with a one-sentence plain-text readback ending with its source in plain words; omit only when numbers are missing.
progress.delivered: list of {item, outcome}; item is "Readable title (owner/repo#123)" plus tag Q4 plan / Q3 carry-over / outside the plan; outcome is one sentence on the intended benefit; claim live/verified only with release or acceptance evidence.
progress.attention: list of at most five {item, why, decision}; item named as above; why matters now, with deadline or "not recorded", and cost of not deciding; decision names one role (and who prepares), optional options sub-bullets with one recommended; dates only when recorded.
progress.retro: optional {keep, change}; each two to four sentences of prose; no per-person metrics.
progress.followUps: list of at most eight {title, context}; title is an imperative task one person can take; context is "Parent: <owner/repo#123> · Owner: <recorded @handle, or proposed role (unassigned)> · due <recorded date, or omit>. Done when <visible end state>."; ordered by risk.
progress.numbers: list of {signal, value}; supporting metrics, folded.
progress.method: list of data sources, collection date and caveats, folded.
--}}
